Switch the gateway single clients use, for example to send one device
through a WireGuard tunnel while the rest of the network uses WAN.

Clients are matched by MAC address, so they stay on DHCP. IPv6 is either
routed through the tunnel (with NAT66) or rejected for the switched client
only. A switched client never falls back to WAN when the tunnel is down.

